        </section><section class="- topic/section ">
            <title class="- topic/title ">User Key Store buttons</title>
            <ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p conref="../reuse/WH-guide-General_0000048987.dita#descGen/buttonView-p" class="- topic/p "/>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p conref="../reuse/WH-guide-General_0000048987.dita#descGen/deviceNew-p" class="- topic/p "/>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Cert Request</uicontrol> opens a <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Certificate Request</wintitle> window, which is used to create a Certificate Signing Request (CSR).</p>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p conref="../reuse/WH-guide-General_0000048987.dita#descGen/buttonDelete-p" class="- topic/p "/>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p conref="../reuse/WH-guide-General_0000048987.dita#descGen/buttonImport-p" class="- topic/p "/>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p conref="../reuse/WH-guide-General_0000048987.dita#descGen/buttonExport-p" class="- topic/p "/>
                    <p class="- topic/p ">For certificates, the file extension is .pem.</p>
                </li><li class="- topic/li ">
                    <p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Reset</uicontrol> deletes all certificates in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">User Key Store</wintitle> and creates a new default certificate. It does not matter which certificate is selected when you click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Reset</uicontrol></p>
                    <note type="caution" class="- topic/note ">
                        <p class="- topic/p ">Do not reset without considering the consequences. The <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Reset</uicontrol> button facilitates creating a new key pair (private and public keys) for the entity, but may disable connections if valid certificates are already in use. Export all certificates before you reset.</p>
                    </note>
                </li></ul>
        </section></refbody></reference>